findings.recommendation:
Register the filter explicitly via a @Bean FilterRegistrationBean<WebhookPayloadSizeFilter> with .setOrder(Ordered.HIGHEST_PRECEDENCE + 10) and .addUrlPatterns("/webhooks/telegram/*"). Drop the @Order on the bean to avoid double-registration ambiguity. Example:

@Bean
public FilterRegistrationBean<WebhookPayloadSizeFilter> webhookPayloadSizeFilterRegistration(WebhookPayloadSizeFilter filter) {
    FilterRegistrationBean<WebhookPayloadSizeFilter> reg = new FilterRegistrationBean<>(filter);
    reg.setOrder(Ordered.HIGHEST_PRECEDENCE + 10);
    reg.addUrlPatterns("/webhooks/telegram/*");
    return reg;
}
